## Commands & Code Examples

```java
// Example 1: Implicit Typecasting with Characters
char ch = 'A';
int x = ch; // Implicit conversion from char to int -> Output: 65
System.out.println(x);

// Example 2: Explicit Typecasting
char pyyush = 'a';
int y = (int) pyyush; // Explicitly casting data type from char to int -> Output: 97
System.out.println(y);

// Example 3: Arithmetic Evaluation & BODMAS Rule
int calculation = 2 * 4 + 6 / 3; 
// Evaluates as: 8 + 2 = 10

// Example 4: Prefix vs Postfix Increment Behavior
int num1 = 10;
System.out.println(++num1); // Prefix: Increments to 11 first, then prints 11

int num2 = 10;
System.out.println(num2++); // Postfix: Prints 10 first, then increments
System.out.println(num2);   // Prints the updated value: 11

// Example 5: Relational Operators and Boolean Data Types
boolean x = (5 > 3);
System.out.println(x); // Evaluates and outputs: true

